 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-074: Exp4327 Either Reproduces ar25 L1 Or Records An Honest E3 Partial
 **Description:** Running Exp 4327 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ar25` when the local ar25 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ar25_L1_reproduced` only when an induced-model plan is executed without trusting a divergent model and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` independently reaches at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ar25_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded model-refinement/planning attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world-model hash, plan, and reproduction result. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve the world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-075: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Executable World Model Exp4328 ka59 Offline Attempt
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4328 as an offline, no-leaderboard E3 executable-world-model attempt on `ka59`, after graph-explore could not crack the mechanic-limited deep-tail game and the executable-world-model SOTA solved it. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/ka59/` is non-empty, that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` imports, and that the task performs no TRM training and does not modify `scripts/research_conductor.py`; if the offline ka59 environment is missing it MUST write `honest_verdict="blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59"` and stop. The workflow MUST use `results/arc_e3/ka59/world_model.py` as the induced model deliverable, score verifier reproduction accuracy over offline `collect_transitions("ka59")` data, print and persist `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, execute any induced-model plan only through the real offline environment, and accept an E3 solve only when `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports at least one reproduced level. If the bounded round budget ends without such a reproduced solve, it MUST still write an honest partial artifact with the best verifier accuracy and a residual missing-world-model-rule gap in `ops/verifier_gaps.md`. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4328_e3_executable_world_model_ka59.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, `world_model_path`, `world_model_sha256`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced or complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>). A reproduced L1 and an honest partial are BOTH progress.`; `verifier_accuracy_per_round` = `list[float]: the verifier's reproduction rate per refactor round -- the trustworthy progress signal for the induced model.`; `world_model_path` = `results/arc_e3/ka59/world_model.py -- the induced model IS the deliverable.`; `world_model_sha256` = `Hash of the induced world model -- auditable/reproducible.`; `offline_reproduced` = `BARE bool: the real env reaches L1 via the induced-model plan, re-gated -- only reproduced levels count.`; `reproduced_levels` = `BARE int: levels offline-reproduced on ka59 (target >=1) -- the +1 incremental-progress unit.`; `plan_executed` = `BARE bool + divergence_step: execution-grounded confirmation; halt-on-divergence.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVE is execution-grounded (real env defines the win); ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world model + the plan + the reproduce() result; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-075: Exp4328 Either Reproduces ka59 L1 Or Records An Honest E3 Partial
+**Description:** Running Exp 4328 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59` when the local ka59 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced` only when an induced-model plan is executed without trusting a divergent model and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` independently reaches at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded model-refinement/planning attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world-model hash, plan, and reproduction result. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve the world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap.
